BASH PARAMETER EXPANSION
→ 005.43 → Shell Programming

Fundamentals
  $VAR          simple expansion
  ${VAR}        braced expansion (safer)
  unset         variable does not exist
  null/empty    variable exists but value is empty
  set           variable has a value (including empty unless noted)

Remove prefix / suffix
  ${parameter%suffix}     remove shortest matching suffix
  ${parameter%%suffix}    remove longest matching suffix
  ${parameter#prefix}     remove shortest matching prefix
  ${parameter##prefix}    remove longest matching prefix

Pattern replace
  ${parameter/pattern/string}     replace first match
  ${parameter//pattern/string}    replace all matches
  ${parameter/%pattern/string}    replace suffix match
  ${parameter/#pattern/string}    replace prefix match

Default values
  ${FOO:-val}    use val if FOO is unset or empty; FOO unchanged
  ${FOO:=val}    set FOO to val if unset or empty
  ${FOO:+val}    use val if FOO is set and not empty; FOO unchanged
  ${FOO:?message}  print message and exit if FOO is unset or empty

Substrings
  ${FOO:0:3}     substring start 0, length 3
  ${FOO:(-3):3}  substring from the right

Length
  ${#FOO}        length of $FOO

String substitutions
  food=
  echo ${food:-Cake}          # Cake   (food empty)

  STR="/path/to/foo.cpp"
  echo ${STR%.cpp}            # /path/to/foo
  echo ${STR%.cpp}.o          # /path/to/foo.o
  echo ${STR%/*}              # /path/to
  echo ${STR##*.}             # cpp
  echo ${STR##*/}             # foo.cpp
  echo ${STR#*/}              # path/to/foo.cpp
  echo ${STR##*/}             # foo.cpp
  echo ${STR/foo/bar}         # /path/to/bar.cpp

String slicing
  name="John"
  echo ${name}                # John
  echo ${name:0:2}            # Jo
  echo ${name::2}             # Jo
  echo ${name: -1}            # n     (space before -)
  echo ${name:(-1)}           # n
  echo ${name:(-2)}           # hn
  echo ${name:(-2):2}         # hn
  length=2
  echo ${name:0:length}       # Jo

String transformation
  STR="HELLO WORLD!"
  echo ${STR,}                # hELLO WORLD!
  echo ${STR,,}               # hello world!

  STR="hello world!"
  echo ${STR^}                # Hello world!
  echo ${STR^^}               # HELLO WORLD!

  ARR=(hello World)
  echo "${ARR[@],}"           # hello world
  echo "${ARR[@]^}"           # Hello World

Basepath and dirpath
  SRC="/path/to/foo.cpp"
  BASEPATH=${SRC##*/}         # foo.cpp
  DIRPATH=${SRC%$BASEPATH}    # /path/to/
